{"symbol":"KGL.WA","area":"poland","updated":"2026-11-09T19:52:36Z","info":{"address1":"ul. Gen. Wladyslawa Sikorskiego 17","city":"Izabelin","zip":"05-080","country":"Poland","phone":"48 22 321 30 00","fax":"48 22 321 3009","website":"https://www.kgl.pl","industry":"Specialty Chemicals","industryKey":"specialty-chemicals","industryDisp":"Specialty Chemicals","sector":"Basic Materials","sectorKey":"basic-materials","sectorDisp":"Basic Materials","longBusinessSummary":"KGL SA engages in the supply of thermoplastic polymer granulates in Poland and internationally. It offers styrenics, such as expandable, and low and high impact polystyrene, as well as styrene-butadiene copolymer; and polyolefins, including polypropylene homopolymer, polypropylene block copolymer, random polypropylene copolymer, metallocene polypropylene, metallocene polyethylene, and ethylene vinyl acetate copolymer, as well as high, medium, and low-density polyethylene. The company also provides engineering plastics, such as polyoxymethylene polyacetal, polycarbonate, polymethyl methacrylate, polyamide, acrylonitrile-styrene-acrylic terpolymer, styrene-acrylonitrile copolymer, acrylonitrile-butadiene-styrene terpolymer, PC/ABS blend, filled polypropylenes, phenylene polysulphide, and polyvinylidene fluoride; and special polymers comprising electrically conductive, thermally conductive, thermally resistant, wear resistant, and high specific gravity thermoplastic composites, as well as filled and reinforced polymers. In addition, it offers elastomers, such as thermoplastic vulcanizate, styrene/ethylene-butylene/styrene terpolymers, and styrene/butadiene/styrene copolymer, as well as dyes, UV stabilizers, antistatic agents, antiblocks, special modifiers, and chalk fillers. Further, the company designs and builds moulds for the thermoforming machines and injection systems; and manufactures packaging and foil products for storage and protection of food products. It is also engaged in manufacturer of plastic food packaging. KGL SA was founded in 1992 and is headquartered in Izabelin, Poland.","fullTimeEmployees":780,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Krzysztof Stanislaw Gromkowski","title":"President of the Management Board","fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":527000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Piotr  Mierzejewski","title":"CFO & Vice President of the Management Board","fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":529,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Ireneusz  Strzelczak","title":"Member of the Supervisory Board","fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":527,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Adam  Skibinski","title":"Vice President of the Management Board","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Rafal  Cybulski","title":"Vice President of the Management Board","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Katarzyna  Lipowska","title":"Chief Accountant","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0}],"compensationAsOfEpochDate":1767139200,"executiveTeam":[],"maxAge":86400,"priceHint":2,"previousClose":13.2,"open":13.2,"dayLow":13.2,"dayHigh":13.2,"regularMarketPreviousClose":13.2,"regularMarketOpen":13.2,"regularMarketDayLow":13.2,"regularMarketDayHigh":13.2,"dividendRate":1,"dividendYield":0,"exDividendDate":1751846400,"payoutRatio":0.4348,"fiveYearAvgDividendYield":1.68,"beta":-0.049,"volume":2,"regularMarketVolume":2,"averageVolume":911,"averageVolume10days":1648,"averageDailyVolume10Day":1648,"bid":12.8,"ask":13.2,"marketCap":93103664,"nonDilutedMarketCap":93103665,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":9,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":13.8,"allTimeHigh":30.9,"allTimeLow":7.8,"fulldayPrice":13.2,"fulldayChange":0,"fulldayChangePercent":0,"priceToSalesTrailing12Months":0.164851,"fiftyDayAverage":11.902,"twoHundredDayAverage":10.8165,"trailingAnnualDividendRate":0,"trailingAnnualDividendYield":0,"currency":"PLN","tradeable":false,"enterpriseV